<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson's Scarus -> Pomacanthus coordinate transformation fitted to real species — Code-to-model traceability: 80/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-17"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Each step is tied to its source as before, and the new section carries the same discipline: the docstring's item 7 says what is segmented, how, and what the anchors are; every segmentation constant (white threshold, background frame, core quantile, texture quantile, box, shadow cut) is a named parameter with a comment saying what it is for; the registration anchors are stated in terms of the dataset's landmark numbers; the figure's row F title names the figure each grid corresponds to. The trace still ends at Thompson's prose and drawing, the oblique/isogonal reading of Fig. 376 is still made by eye, and the declared box for the field photograph is a judgement recorded rather than derived." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-code-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-code-traceability-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-code-traceability-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-code-traceability-5> ;
    pk:hasScore 8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson's Scarus -> Pomacanthus coordinate transformation fitted to real species — Model fidelity to source: 78/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-17"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "As before: \"coaxial circles\" formalised as the Moebius group with the reading stated, the oblique family added for Fig. 376 as drawn, the alternatives Thompson compares against (rectilinear coordinates) and does not (affine) fitted the same way, the thin-plate spline of Bookstein 1989 as the exact deformation, fitters checked on synthetic maps. Raised because the thing Thompson actually deformed - an outline - is now carried by each family and compared with a real outline, so curvature between the landmarks is no longer untested, and because the test is set up so that his family can only win by beating the no-deformation baseline, which is the comparison his sentence makes (\"rectilinear co-ordinates\" -> \"coaxial circles\" -> \"a very good outline\"). Not higher because his drawn grid is still displayed, not digitised and compared constant by constant; because the landmark test rests on genus means and the outline test on one individual per species, so neither is his \"typical Scaroid fish\"; and because the maps are fitted to the landmarks and only applied to the outline, so a map fitted to the outline itself (semilandmarks) is not tried." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-model-fidelity-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-model-fidelity-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-model-fidelity-6> ;
    pk:hasScore 7.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson's Scarus -> Pomacanthus coordinate transformation fitted to real species — Morphometric validation: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-17"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "To the landmark validation of the first audit (Procrustes distance, residual and explained share per family, within-genus noise floor, leave-one-landmark-out, depth/length and singular-value ratio, per-landmark residuals, all 3782 genus pairs, Scarus -> Chaetodon) the outline test adds two measurements on real silhouettes - IoU of the filled outlines and mean symmetric boundary distance - for every family against an explicit no-deformation baseline, so the question \"does the map help on the outline\" has a number and the answer is no for all five. The sidecar re-derives the IoU with a different rasteriser (agreement to 0.0001) and records the silhouette areas and the peduncle-anchor positions (0.79 and 0.84 of length). Not higher because there is still no published value to compare against (nobody has fitted this pair), one individual per species gives the outline numbers no spread, and digitising error on the landmarks is still not estimated." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
