    rdfs:label "Thompson's Scarus -> Pomacanthus coordinate transformation fitted to real species — MorphoEval overall 76.6/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-17"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Landmark test as in the 2026-10-16 audit, unchanged in code and numbers: 791 species x 17 landmarks, hash-checked; generalised Procrustes superimposition; from the Scarus genus mean to the Pomacanthus genus mean the similarity (0.0312), affine (0.0259, 31 % explained), Moebius (0.0311, 0.8 %), oblique coaxial (0.0256, 32 %) and thin-plate spline (exact, bending energy 0.678) fits, with the within-genus noise floor (Pomacanthus 0.0132), leave-one-landmark-out (0.0371), depth/length (0.377 -> 0.587), all 3782 genus pairs (this pair at the 31st percentile) and Scarus -> 54 Chaetodon species (median 35 %). New: the real-outline test. Two Commons photographs are fetched and hash-checked; the Scarus ghobban specimen is segmented by its Lab distance from white, the living Pomacanthus semicirculatus by a marker watershed (Mahalanobis colour distance from the frame-sampled sand plus colour gradient; markers are the declared box's outside and the 1.5 % least sand-like pixels plus the most textured pixels in their convex hull; shadow cleared below 0.745 of the height). Each silhouette is registered to its species' 17 landmarks by a similarity through two anchors the silhouette gives (snout -> LM2, caudal peduncle -> LM5-LM6 midpoint; the peduncle is tracked from the tail tip as the first local minimum of thickness between caudal fin and body). The five maps are fitted to the S. ghobban -> P. semicirculatus landmarks and applied to the Scarus silhouette; against the Pomacanthus silhouette the IoU is similarity 0.662, affine 0.652, Moebius 0.645, oblique coaxial 0.618, thin-plate spline 0.629, and the mean symmetric boundary distance 5.6, 6.5, 5.9, 7.0 and 6.6 % of body length. Second figure: the two photographs with silhouette, placed landmarks and anchors; both silhouettes in the Procrustes frame; five panels of the carried Scarus outline over the real Pomacanthus outline (with the coaxial and TPS grids); a bar chart of IoU and boundary distance with the similarity baseline marked; the caveats in the figure. --no-photos skips it. Overall 76.6/100 (faithfulness 74.3, reproducibility 82.0); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 232e8f8; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0, scikit-image 0.26.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 78, Morphological realism / specimen match 72, Parameter expressivity 55, Morphometric validation 86, Source and data traceability 92, Code-to-model traceability 80, Reproducibility package 75. Output judged: thompson_scarus_pomacanthus.png: rendered output of thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py at 232e8f8, image/png, 739620 B, 2520×1540 px, artifact_sha256 d243f51e2b90b1a2201ec81265392b1cf95ea0f0e6e68074818cc5754b324e08 (sha256 d243f51e2b90b1a2201ec81265392b1cf95ea0f0e6e68074818cc5754b324e08). Supersedes audit: 2026-10-16-thompson-audit." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Add more individuals per species (several Commons photographs each, or the Bishop Museum photographs the landmarks were digitised on) so the outline IoU has a spread, and prefer specimens in the same posture (both collected, or both living).",
        "remediation needed: Digitise Thompson's drawn grid of Fig. 376 from the pinned scan, fit the Moebius constants to it, and compare them with the constants fitted to the species, so his drawing is tested and not only his family.",
        "remediation needed: Estimate digitising error (replicate landmarking of a few photographs) so the noise floor can be separated into species and measurement variance.",
        "remediation needed: Fit the maps to the outlines themselves (sliding semilandmarks on the two silhouettes) as well as to the landmarks, so Thompson's family gets its best chance on the form he deformed.",
        "remediation needed: Pin the Python 3.14 environment (exact versions) in requirements or a lock file.",
        "remediation needed: Sweep the complex constant c at fixed affine part in a panel, and report the fitted constants for the 54 Chaetodon species to test \"small variations in the values of the constants\" directly." ;
    pk:hasScore 7.66e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson's Scarus -> Pomacanthus coordinate transformation fitted to real species — Parameter expressivity: 55/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-17"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Unchanged. The GIF moves the eight constants of the oblique family from the identity to the fitted values and shows the grid bending into coaxial circles while the fish deepens; the Chaetodont claim is tested by fitting the family to each of the 54 Chaetodon species. The constants are still not swept one at a time, the fitted constants for the Chaetodon species are not reported, and the outline test adds nothing here (it applies fitted maps, it does not vary constants)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-parameter-expressivity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-parameter-expressivity-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 5.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-repro-package> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson's Scarus -> Pomacanthus coordinate transformation fitted to real species — Reproducibility package: 75/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-17"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Deterministic, invocation and outputs documented, data file in the repository and hash-checked; the two new network fetches are optional (--no-photos), hash-checked, cached and need only Pillow and scikit-image, both in requirements.txt; re-runs give identical numbers. Unchanged score: the environment is still recorded only in this audit (lower bounds in requirements.txt), the GIF still takes ~2 min, and the outline test adds ~30 s and a dependency on two third-party URLs remaining byte-stable (Commons originals have been; the hashes will refuse a changed file rather than silently use it)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/repro-package" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-repro-package-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-repro-package-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-repro-package-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 7.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-source-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson's Scarus -> Pomacanthus coordinate transformation fitted to real species — Source and data traceability: 92/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-17"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "As before - Thompson to page and figure with the scan pinned to one leaf; the landmark table to its Dryad DOI, licence and byte size, vendored and hash-checked; landmark definitions to Claverie & Wainwright Fig. 1; Bookstein 1978 and 1989 - and now the two photographs are cited to their Commons pages, photographers, institutional or Flickr source ids and licences (CC BY 4.0, CC BY 2.0), pinned by SHA-256 in the script and the dataset README, with the credits printed in the figure. Short of full marks for the same two reasons: the landmark semantics were read off a figure, and the Dryad download could not be scripted." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-source-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/source-traceability" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-source-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-source-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-source-traceability-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-source-traceability-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-source-traceability-5> ;
    pk:hasScore 9.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson's Scarus -> Pomacanthus coordinate transformation fitted to real species — Morphological realism / specimen match: 72/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-17"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The side-by-side the dimension asks for is now made with real animals: a photographed Scarus ghobban and a photographed Pomacanthus semicirculatus, their silhouettes drawn on the photographs with the dataset's landmarks placed on them so the registration can be checked by eye, and in row F the parrotfish outline carried by each family laid over the angelfish outline, with the gap visible - the angelfish's trailing dorsal and anal lobes and deeper belly are left by every map. Thompson's own figure is still placed beside the data from the pinned scan, and the 791 species remain the specimens of the landmark test. Judged on the match, the carried fish does not become a Pomacanthus: IoU 0.618 for his family against 0.662 with no deformation. Not higher because there is one individual per species, a dead specimen on white against a living fish on a reef (fin posture is declared as a confound, not controlled), the field silhouette depends on a declared box and shadow cut, and the landmarks are placed on the photographs by two anchors rather than digitised on them - so the picture is honest but the specimen pair is not yet a measured one." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-specimen-match-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-specimen-match-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-specimen-match-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-specimen-match-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-specimen-match-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-specimen-match-6> ;
    pk:hasScore 7.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

